      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-11-02_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <head>FAMOUS FEMALE</head>
        <p>FAMOUS FEMALE</p>
        <p>BOOK FOR MARRIED WOMEN</p>
        <p>The information contained in this book ought to be know. by every married woman, cud it will not bana the unmarriep to read. The book is conveniently divided into it chapters The first chapter treats of the changes at puberty, or when a girl becomes a woman. The seoond chapter treats of marriage from a doctor's standpoint ; points out the best age for marriage, and who should have children and who not, and furnishes useful information that one can ordinarily get only from an intell•gent doctor. The third chapter treats of the marriage of blood relations; and condemns suck marriages as a rule. Chapter four treats of the signs of pregnancy. The Ifth chapter tells how a woman should live during the pregnant state. Toe tittle chapter treats f mishaps and how to avoid them. The seventh chapter treats of maternal impressions and shows that birthmarks are not due to longings on the part of the mother, but rather to her poor health. The eighth chapter teaches how to have easy sonfinements. Certain people believe that women should bring forth in pain and trouble, but the hygienic physician says that conlnements can be made oomparativsly easy if oertain rules are obeyed ; these rules are given. The ninth chapter treats of the proper management of confinement until the baby is born. The tenth chapter tells how to treat he mother till she Is up and about again. The eleventh chapter treats of sterility ; gives the main causes of it, how these may be overcome and children result. The last chapter treats of the "change," a most Important article for all women aver forty. The book is full of useful information and no book is written which goes so thoroughly into matters relating to married women. Some may think too much is told ; such can scarcely be the ca.e. for knowledge is power and the means is' attaining happiness. The book can be nal from Dr. T. R. ALLINSON, 25 Box, 4, Spanish-place Manchester-square, London, W., in return for a Postal Order for is. id</p>
        <p>MACKENZIE'S FEMALE REMEDY. One case guaranteed to remove the most OBSTINATB OBARUCTICNS and IRREGULARITIES in 12 hours. HARMLESS. Nothing can re.ist it. Failure is impossible Bead stamped envelope for PARTICULARS. TBSTI- MONIALS, and ADVICE. Ours is the most POWERFUL and STRONGEST Remedy Sold, and in no single caw. has it ever failed—even In the m3st longstanding, intricate, and lingering cases. Post tree, under cover, with written guarantee of cure Ss. (five shillings).—Mrs. W. B. MACKENZIE. Trafford House, 83. Dawes-road, Fulham, London. Mention paper. •</p>
        <p>~.'",.....7.:"..':...:'.;.'...,...''.:7::."':-',...,.'.1i.-....2,.::•,:-"t..:1"":.,?.....,,.".:'"'".7","...:...:-.':.7::.4...7."."''',.,..,:'''f;',;::''...t......i.......,7::</p>
