        <p>FURNITURE BY GOODALL. FURNITURE. BY GILLOW. FURNITURE BY OGDBN. FURNITURR BY LAMB. FURNITURE BY MAPIE. IURNIIURE BY eHOOLDREID. FURNITURE BY GARNETT. Lc., *C.</p>
        <p>The extensive alterations ne.ce.sitated by eon; ibued in- crease of business having now been almost comple ed. the Proprietors have pleasure in informing their old-established " clienfel " and the public generatly that the increased Exhibition Space in their Showrooms (opposite all S dote' Church) has enabled them to stock and display an enorm- ously added Qtantity of FUSNITU ll—both new and Second-hand—so that thei- Cu-tomers have now a Collection to choose from. which it is not to much to say is second to none in the United Kingdom. IVidist, of course, the Market is being flooded with new Modern Furniture, there scarcely was a time when High-class, :second-hand, Durab'e and Handsome SUITES were more difficult to cootailt. But ever on the alert, the first in tee field, we are glad to say that we have been successful in securing one of the rarest and completest Collections of every variay of Furniture ever offer el to the public since we entered the Trade. Thes- corn- prise 1-1. The Household Furniture of a Wesleyan Minister near Manchester, who has mealy been appointed to the Foreign Missions. 2. The establishment of a issit,ing heavy weight jockey, who is about to start as a Roan Country Trainer. 3. The Household lifferts of an ex-M.P in Staffordshire, who has been ordered abroad account of ill- health. 4. Seven Houses of Furniture from Sidou,ban Villas and Mansions sold under writs of " Seri liacia,," and purclnaed by GULDSTONR and SONS ; the whole compris- ing the moat Magnificent and hlaborate bele&amp; ion ever seen in Mancl,eater (part already spoken fur) and Now on View. " Chef d'reuvree by the most Celebrated Makers. Furni- ture in Chippendale, Sheraton and Antique Oak. Furniture he Ash, Birch, Maple, Walnut, iiosewood, and !Asir:zany. £10,C03 OP NRWLT-ADDBD STOCK. Now on offer at aear4 one-halt its original value. Railway Fares Paid to Country Customers. Catalogths Free on Ap plhAtion.</p>
        <p>THOSE ABOUT TO MARRY and those who contemplate adding to their present Stock of Furniture are specially invited to pay an early visit ti the Manchester Louvre (opp,roite All Saints' Chur-h). Advice gratis on the choice ant selection of EVERY RIQUISITH FOR COTTAGE OR MANSION. Parties visiting Ooldstone and Sons, should ent,r the Ox- ford-at., Ruiholaic, or Wlttiltigtofl ear at Piooadil,y, and ask the conductor to stop at GOLDSTONE AND SONS, where they will be aetonibhed to And such spacious and eiegazitly-api,ointed Showrooms. surpassing anything out- side of London. Do not forget that we now hold TUNI OT COMPLME COLLECTION OP FURNITURE EYRE OFFREED, AT ABOUT 0114-11 ALF ITS ORIGINAL COST. Absolutely unapproach.ble tor Islegauce, Comfort, ' Durability. All goods are polished and turned out without a blemish as good as yawn new. We give Credit when required and only charge a small per'entage .1 the convenienoe. Railway Fair paid to Country Customers and all goods - delivered free.</p>
        <p>THIS WEEK'S LIST OF SECOND-RAND BARGAINS. £3 108., worth £l5. Solid Waluut CABINET, with large bevel plate-gisi4 back, fitted with Cupboard, Shelv.s. Au. £4 15s. Very massive solid Mahogany SIDE SOAR°. originally cosf over £'2,o. Large plate-glass back, Cupboards, Drawers. Cellarette, and all toe mod-rn i!ouveniences ; just beeu re-polished. RS b. uraud Mahogany OMISSIVE, 6fl long, very bi:.ll carved baok, fitted with all Drawers and Lrass handles. Werth £25. £4 15s. Very hindsome Parlour SUITE, in real Leather. beautifully upholstered, consisting Couch, pair of 'merge Easy Chairs and tour Small Chairs all Pith padded becks. A Harg.,in. Cost, wheu new, £25. Eel lbs., worth £3O. Solid DRAWING-ROOSi, neatly upholstered In dark coloured itepp ; just bten e-upholstered emu re-poliehed. This lot includes Couch, Lady's and Gent.'s Easy Chairs anl six 311X1 di Chair., all spring seats. £1 15s. Beiut,fuliilaii tiHMFONIMt. with real Marble Top, all Cupboards, and thoroughly well lied,hed. A bar- gain for double the money. £3 lts. Pair of elegantly constructed TOILET TABLES. all Rued with Drawers, Swing-glass, Tile Back, and Towel hafl oumbined. Delivered free.</p>
