        <p>GLADYS "Why are you going to all that trouble to open that letter so very carefully, Vivian?" Vivian: "Oh I had a quarrel with Mr. Lighthead, and intend to send back his letter unopened; but I just thought I would see what he said before I returned it" PROFESSIONAL INsrixer.—Husband (the father of six laughters) : "Come, Rosa there is a gentleown in the &amp;awing-room who wants to marry one of our daughters. He is a wine mer- chnnt." Wife: A wine merchant? Heaven be praised I Then he will be sure to select one of the older brands." THE Rev. Party: I hear, Smith, that you have left our Sunday-school, and joined another. What is the reason?" Smith : "Well, 'cos I heard that you wal a-going to hold the summer treat in a field like you did last year. So I just goes and joins the other school, 'cos they is a-going to the seaside at Remsgate for their treat." Maul): I should not mind Mr. Steighlait's calling upon me so much if he would go home earlier. Mary (affectionately) : Why don't you play to him, dearest?</p>
