        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT ASSOCIATION OF YOUNG PEOPLE'S SOCIETIES OF CHRISTIAN ENDEAVOUR. THE AUTUMNAL CONVENTION Will be held (D.V.) in EMMANUEL REFORMED CHURCH OF ENGLAND, BOLD ST., WARRINGTON, On SATURDAY NEX r. OCT. 12th. 1895, At 2.30 and 6.0 p.m. Rev. W. H. TOWERS, President of the Manchester and District Union, Rev. JAMES MURSELL, Derby, Who will give an address on his recent visit to the great International Convention in Boston, U.S.A., HENRY HUTCHINSON. ESQ., Organising Secretary Children's Special Service Mission, W. H. HOPE, ESQ. Vice-President of the Liverpool and District Union, MRS. HIGGS, President of the Oldham and District Association, JOHN CRUMBLEHULME, Escl., of Bolton, And others are expected to take part. Special Christian Endeavour Hymns will be sung. The meetings are open to all. Friends interested in Sunday School and other work amongst the young are very cordially invited. Tea will be provided at 5 o'clock in the Schoolroom over Arpley Station at a charge of 6d. each. Collection at the evening meeting to defray expenses.</p>
